{
  "additional_concerns": [
    "Footnote 3 is supplied in da12aecad4e68.u30.3569: \"Hongkong Post e-Cert (electronic certificate) is required for this submission.\" Its markers attach to XML and PDF, not the web form. The web-form claim's missing-footnote uncertainty is stale; neither an additional web-form e-Cert requirement nor a general authentication exemption follows.",
    "node.5d8c4ca625a46c41ff2f4098 includes filings before 9:00am on 2 February 2026. The source distinguishes the calendar-date channel rule from the operational launch and resubmission \"following its implementation\". Preserve the competing temporal interpretations; these predicates are not equivalent.",
    "The instant-based candidates adopt an inclusive 9:00am threshold. The supplied source does not expressly identify the governing timezone or settle exact-boundary inclusion. Authoritative clarification is missing, with no identifiable supplied dependency mapping.",
    "The blackout provision permits urgent direct contact. Contact alone does not establish submission, but contact could result in an actual filing. This provision does not establish general permission to use other channels after launch.",
    "node.29b224046d115582fbf223fb puts actual submission in the result; the other event candidates put it in scope. A non-filing can therefore yield FALSE versus OUT_OF_SCOPE. Whether this matters depends on the admissible input domain.",
    "The history candidate delegates event existence and sufficient-history assessment to an external Boolean. The formula does not verify completeness or connect the responsible entity's licensed status to each historical submitter.",
    "TRUE_IS_SATISFIED must retain the typed DUTY_TRIGGER meaning. Later resubmission does not erase an earlier triggering event; these questions do not determine whether the duty remains outstanding.",
    "Neither web-form permission nor XML liaison is an additional resubmission-trigger prerequisite. Adding either would impose an unsupported restriction. Conversely, a false trigger result does not authorize another channel.",
    "The separately provided XML schema and promised resubmission guidance are absent, and their opaque dependency IDs cannot be reliably identified. Their contents are unnecessary for the two narrow claims assessed here and must not be inferred.",
    "All nine required pairs are retained. NOT_APPLICABLE findings concern these specific claim-question relationships; they neither establish overall candidate correctness nor authorize pruning."
  ],
